ers and existing clinical models, highlighting the potential of this stratification approach to enable more precise and personalized diagnosis by capturing the underlying heterogeneity of CMVD. This work represents the first application of imaging-based endotyping and the integration of genetic and proteomic data for CMVD risk prediction, establishing a framework for multimodal modeling in complex diseases.",exclude_uncertain_unstable,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,primary_model_paper,no,no,no,no,,,,,"The abstract describes integration of imaging, proteomics, and polygenic risk scores for risk prediction, with no mention of natural-language text or a text‑bio mapping. | The abstract focuses on risk prediction, classification, and unsupervised endotyping without any reference to generative mechanisms such as decoder, autoregressive, or diffusion models.","The abstract describes integration of imaging, proteomics, and polygenic risk scores for risk prediction, with no mention of natural-language text or a text‑bio mapping.","The abstract focuses on risk prediction, classification, and unsupervised endotyping without any reference to generative mechanisms such as decoder, autoregressive, or diffusion models.",
