d applicability to confirm foundation-model characteristics.","evidence_snippet":"\"a single-cell foundation model can perform this translation via adversarial fine-tuning\""},{"record_id":"rec_000092","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"PlantGFM is explicitly described as a genomic foundation model with pretraining on 10.84 billion nucleotides. The abstract states that it supports sequence generation and de novo design.","evidence_snippet":"\"pre-trained on 10.84 billion nucleotides\"; \"supports long-context ... prediction and sequence generation\"; \"de novo design of novel candidates\""},{"record_id":"rec_000093","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"DamageFormer is presented as a multimodal detection/localization framework, and LesionBERT is a damage-aware genomic foundation model. The abstract does not show a genuinely generative architecture, despite transfer to unseen lesion types.","evidence_snippet":"\"damage-aware genomic foundation model built upon DNABERT-2\"; \"framework for detection and localization of DNA lesions\"; \"generalizes to chemically distinct guanine lesions\""},{"record_id":"rec_000094","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a single-cell transcriptome profiling and expression-atlas/resource paper, not a model paper. The abstract contains no generative architecture or foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"comprehensive single-cell transcriptome profiling\"; \"provides an enhanced type 2 diabetes expression-atlas\"; \"novel genomic resource\""},{"record_id":"rec_000095","paper_type":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a spatial transcriptomics/scRNA-seq biology study and validation of cell states, not a generative model. It does not provide foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"We describe the use of true single-cell resolution spatial transcriptomics\"; \"identify and localize key transcriptional programs in situ\""},{"record_id":"rec_000096","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SI-SimCLR is a self-supervised representation-learning framework for reconstructing phenotypic landscapes, but the abstract does not describe a generative model. It also lacks evidence of foundation-model-style pretraining or broad transfer.","evidence_snippet":"\"self-supervised learning framework\"; \"learns biologically informative representations\"; \"enables reconstruction of cellular phenotypic landscapes\""}]}
