c models. It summarizes existing recurrence and RFS prediction studies rather than describing a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“We performed a contemporary systematic review”"},{"record_id":"rec_000112","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract applies pre-trained immune system models and a peripheral immune system encoder to predict response and toxicity. This is an application of existing foundation-like models, not a new generative model.","evidence_snippet":"“pre-trained immunotype models” and “a peripheral immune system encoder trained on the BostonGene patient database”"}]}
