oundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"ppIRIS is presented as a deep learning framework to predict PPIs from sequence, which is a discriminative prediction task. The abstract does not describe a generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"predict PPIs directly from sequence\" and \"deep learning framework\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000061","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"ProteomeLM is a transformer-based language model trained on entire proteomes across diverse species, which supports foundation-model-like evidence. However, the abstract describes masked reconstruction rather than a clearly generative decoder or autoregressive model.","evidence_snippet":"\"trained to reconstruct masked protein embeddings\" and \"operates on entire proteomes from species spanning the tree of life\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000062","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract states this is a review of how genomic, environmental, and phenomic information can be integrated. It does not present a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review examines\" integration of genomic, environmental, and phenomic information."},{"record_id":"rec_000063","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work centers on a prediction algorithm that integrates a pretrained protein-language model with gene weights for pathway-level inference. That is an application of an existing model, not evidence of a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrating a pretrained protein-language model and gene weights\" to \"establish a prediction algorithm\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000064","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of emerging multimodal models and AI foundation models in epilepsy, not a primary generative model paper. The abstract summarizes examples and challenges rather than introducing a model.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this review, we summarise\" and \"We describe AI foundation models\"."}]}
