ract clearly describes a comprehensive review of RNA-binding proteins in neuroinflammation. It does not present a model, let alone a generative or foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“This review systematically organizes” and “The review aims to construct a comprehensive theoretical framework”"},{"record_id":"rec_000240","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"The paper studies LLM-based generation of visualization grammars, so a generative workflow is present. But it is an agentic authoring/application paper, and the abstract does not establish foundation-model-style pretraining for a candidate text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“vanilla LLM generation” and “All schemes use the Gosling visualization grammar as structured output”"}]}
