ric stability metric, Shesha\"; \"scGPT foundation model embeddings\""},{"record_id":"rec_000212","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a probing benchmark for frozen DNA encoders, not a generative model paper. It evaluates what is linearly recoverable from embeddings rather than proposing a foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"a lightweight probing benchmark for testing whether frozen DNA embeddings can recover\""},{"record_id":"rec_000213","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract applies existing single-cell foundation models by fine-tuning Geneformer and scGPT on cancer subtypes. It explicitly frames them as transferable representations with out-of-domain generalization.","evidence_snippet":"\"we fine-tuned two widely used scFMs, Geneformer and scGPT\"; \"transferable representations of cellular state\""},{"record_id":"rec_000214","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This paper benchmarks existing single-cell foundation models for RNA-seq integration rather than introducing a new generative model. The abstract is comparative and evaluation-focused.","evidence_snippet":"\"We benchmarked leading single-cell foundation models\" against baselines for data integration"},{"record_id":"rec_000215","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"LAIOR is described as a variational autoencoder with ODE and geometric regularization, so it is generative. However, the abstract does not indicate broad pretraining or foundation-model-like transferability.","evidence_snippet":"\"Lorentz attentive ... variational autoencoder (VAE)\" and \"unified variational framework\""},{"record_id":"rec_000216","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this is a review of multi-agent systems and foundational models. It does not describe a specific generative candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review argues\" and \"We first examine recent foundational models\""}]}
