./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1601:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:1816:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2193:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0016.stderr.log:135:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000121","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly describes autoregressive generation and “bidirectional unification of cell interpretation and generation.” It also states the model is built on Qwen3-4B with continued pretraining, supervised fine-tuning, and reinforcement learning.","evidence_snippet":"“continuous embeddings preclude autoregressive generation” ... “bidirectional unification of cell interpretation and generation”; “Built on Qwen3-4B and trained via continued pretraining”"},{"record_id":"rec_000122","paper_type":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a multimodal analysis of histamine pathway networks, not a model paper. No generative architecture or foundation-model-like training is described.","evidence_snippet":"“We conducted a multimodal analysis ... to map the architecture of the histaminergic system”"},{"record_id":"rec_000123","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a predictive drug-repurposing framework with GNNs and Transformers, but not a genuinely generative model. It focuses on screening and predictive accuracy rather than generation or broad foundation-model pretraining.","evidence_snippet":"“deep learning framework” ... “computationally screened” ... “achieved state-of-the-art predictive accuracy”"},{"record_id":"rec_000124","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract present a review of AI and multi-omics in microbiome research. No original generative model or foundation model is described.","evidence_snippet":"title states “A review”; abstract synthesizes “AI-empowered approaches” and “Emerging opportunities”"},{"record_id":"rec_000125","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a prognostic risk assessment system that outputs a risk score from genomic and clinical features. The abstract does not describe a generative architecture or foundation-model-style pretraining.","evidence_snippet":"“prognostic risk assessment model” ... “the prognostic risk score was output after cross-modal fusion”"},{"record_id":"rec_000126","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The work integrates neural topic modeling with LLMs to create concept-level representations, but the abstract does not clearly state a generative architecture. It also lacks evidence of broad pretraining or other foundation-model characteristics for scConcept itself.","evidence_snippet":"“integrating neural topic modeling with LLMs” ... “transforms gene-level topic representations into structured, human-interpretable biological concepts”"},{"record_id":"rec_000127","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract calls it a transformer-based cfDNA language model, but the described task is lymphoma detection and the generative mechanism is not explicit. There is no evidence of broad pretraining or foundation-model-like scale.","evidence_snippet":"“transformer-based cfDNA language model designed for lymphoma detection” ... “trained on a cohort of 389 samples”"},{"record_id":"rec_000128","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a leakage-controlled prediction system for within-species protein expression, not a generative model. It emphasizes predictive performance and deployment ladders, without broad foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“Aiki-XP predicts within-species relative abundance” ... “leakage-controlled gene-operon split” ... “predicts”"}]}
