ed on plant genomes, which is foundation-model-like evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"CNN and a transformer-based genomic language model pre-trained on plant genomes to predict changes in gene expression\""},{"record_id":"rec_000196","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an application of DNABERT embeddings for DNA sequence alignment, not a new generative model. The abstract frames DNABERT as the existing large language model component in a downstream workflow.","evidence_snippet":"\"combining deep learning with DNABERT embeddings\"; \"large transformer-based language model\"; \"DNA sequence alignment\""},{"record_id":"rec_000197","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"SYMOL is described as a self-supervised multimodal representation-learning framework for spatial transcriptomics integration, not a generative architecture. The abstract does not clearly establish that SYMOL itself has foundation-model-like pretraining or broad transferable scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"unified synergistic self-supervised multimodal framework\"; \"integrates spatial coordinates, gene expression, and histological images\"; uses \"pretrained large vision models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000198","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of AI in early cancer detection rather than a primary model paper. It summarizes CNNs and transformer-based models but does not present a candidate generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review summarizes recent progress and clinical applications of AI\"; \"including Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and Transformer-based models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000199","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a benchmarking guideline and new evaluation tasks for spatial transcriptomics foundation models. It is a benchmark/resource paper, not a generative model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"A practical guideline for benchmarking unimodal and multimodal foundation models\"; \"introduce a new set of tasks and metrics\""},{"record_id":"rec_000200","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a multimodal survival prediction system that outputs risk scores and survival times, so it is predictive rather than generative. The abstract describes modality encoders and fusion, not a foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"multimodal deep learning framework for patient-level survival prediction\"; \"outputs continuous risk scores\"; \"feedforward encoders\""}]}
