l deep generative model. The abstract describes integration, denoising, and imputation, but not broad pretraining or other foundation-model-like evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"hierarchical multimodal deep generative model\"; \"facilitating integration, denoising and imputation tasks\""},{"record_id":"rec_000220","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a multimodal predictive framework using Transformer and GNN architectures for recurrence prediction. The abstract provides no generative mechanism or foundation-model-style pretraining evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"MF-DNN combining Transformer and Graph Neural Network (GNN) architectures decoded the cross-modal electro-metabolic interactions\"; \"AUC of 0.91 for one-year recurrence prediction\""},{"record_id":"rec_000221","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a systematic methodological survey of single-cell foundation models. It reviews architectures, pretraining strategies, and benchmarking challenges rather than presenting a new model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review provides a systematic methodological survey of existing scFMs\""},{"record_id":"rec_000222","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"GeneLLM is a transfer-learning framework built on a pre-trained LLaMA-7B backbone for sepsis classification. The abstract shows foundation-model use, but the application is a downstream diagnostic wrapper rather than a new generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"large language model-based framework\"; \"pre-trained LLaMA-7B backbone