han a new generative model. No evidence is given that the candidate model itself has foundation-model-like pretraining or transfer properties.","evidence_snippet":"\"couples large language model based prior elicitation\" and \"ChatGPT-4o is queried\""},{"record_id":"rec_000044","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"EvoRMD combines RNA language model embeddings with metadata and a shared classifier, which reads as an application built on top of a pretrained model rather than a generative architecture. The abstract does not establish foundation-model-like characteristics for the candidate system.","evidence_snippet":"\"combines RNA language model embeddings\" and \"A shared multiclass classifier produces... predictions\""},{"record_id":"rec_000045","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this is a review that synthesizes advances in Spatial AI and graph neural networks. It is not presenting a new generative model or foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review synthesizes advances in Spatial AI\" and \"The discussion addresses\""},{"record_id":"rec_000046","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model is a predictive multimodal fusion system using XGBoost, CNNs, VAEs, and a Transformer-based fusion network. The abstract provides no evidence of a genuinely generative architecture or foundation-model-like pretraining.","evidence_snippet":"\"A Transformer-based fusion network was employed for joint prediction\" and \"develop a multimodal... prediction model\""},{"record_id":"rec_000047","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"scLLMDA uses a pretrained DNA language model as an embedding source for cell type annotation, which is an applied downstream system rather than a generative model. The abstract does not describe broad pretraining or other foundation-model evidence for the candidate method itself.","evidence_snippet":"\"uses a pretrained DNA-specific language model to generate contextual embeddings\" and \"cell type annotation\""},{"record_id":"rec_000048","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"M-GNN is a multi-modal graph neural network for cancer driver gene prediction, which is predictive rather than generative. The mention of a pre-trained teacher model is distillation support, not evidence of a foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"A multi-modal GNN framework for cancer driver gene prediction\" and \"using soft labels from a pre-trained teacher model\""}]}
