-based VAE, but does not establish broad pretraining or other clear foundation-model-like characteristics for PhAME itself.","evidence_snippet":"\"latent diffusion framework\" and \"latent space of a pretrained graph-based VAE\""},{"record_id":"rec_000100","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a gradient-boosting ensemble for viral genome classification, which is predictive rather than generative. The abstract provides no evidence of foundation-model-style pretraining or transferable representations.","evidence_snippet":"\"automated viral genome classification\" and \"gradient boosting ensemble model\""},{"record_id":"rec_000101","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a multimodal foundation model with large-scale pretraining on 1.76 billion paired samples and transferable downstream uses. However, it does not describe a generative architecture such as a decoder, autoregressive, or diffusion model.","evidence_snippet":"\"multimodal foundation model\" and \"for pretraining, we assembled histMol, a large-scale corpus of 1.76 billion paired...\""},{"record_id":"rec_000102","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"MIST is described as a plug-in replacement for an MIL projection layer that uses paired spatial transcriptomics during training. This is an application wrapper around existing MIL/foundation-model features rather than a generative model or a foundation model itself.","evidence_snippet":"\"plug-in replacement for the MIL projection layer\" and \"uses paired spatial transcriptomics only during training\""},{"record_id":"rec_000103","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract indicate a review of current and future AI applications in surgery, not an original model paper. No generative or foundation-model evidence is presented.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review evaluates and critically analyzes current... applications of AI in surgery\""},{"record_id":"rec_000104","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SpaRank is a transferable deconvolution framework, but the abstract frames it as inference on ranked feature sequences rather than a generative model. It does provide evidence of foundation-model-like transfer through pretrain-transfer behavior and cross-context generalization.","evidence_snippet":"\"adapting the rank-based encodings of single-cell foundation models\" and \"enabling a pretrain-transfer paradigm\""}]}
