./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1640:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:2078:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2507:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0019.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000145","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a systematic evaluation of 11 genomic language models and critiques their pretraining paradigm, rather than presenting a new model. It does not clearly specify a generative architecture or broader foundation-model properties.","evidence_snippet":"“systematically evaluated 11 representative gLMs” and “canonical sequence-only self-supervised pretraining paradigm”"},{"record_id":"rec_000146","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Gemini Pro is used zero-shot as an existing LLM to make ranked primary-site predictions, so this is an application wrapper rather than a new model paper. The abstract explicitly identifies it as a large language model used without fine-tuning.","evidence_snippet":"“Large Language Models (LLMs), such as Gemini Pro” and “zero-shot prompt”"},{"record_id":"rec_000147","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a broad review of AI in drug discovery, not a primary generative model paper. It mentions generative models in passing, but the abstract does not describe a specific generative architecture or foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“This review provides a comprehensive analysis” and “generative models such as GANs and reinforcement learning”"},{"record_id":"rec_000148","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents SciCore-Omics as a tri-modal foundation model trained on a large paired image-gene-text dataset. It also reports zero-shot generalization and language-grounded outputs, supporting both generative and foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“the first tri-modal foundation model linking histology images, spatial transcriptomics, and biological language” and “robust zero-shot generalization”"},{"record_id":"rec_000149","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a review of AI-driven ASD diagnosis across modalities and methods. It does not describe a new generative architecture or provide foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“This review provides a comprehensive analysis” and “deep learning, traditional machine learning, and multimodal fusion techniques”"},{"record_id":"rec_000150","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"GRNPred is an encoder-based graph transformer with masked gene-expression reconstruction and supervised edge prediction, which is predictive rather than clearly generative. The abstract does describe self-supervised pretraining on unlabeled data, but not a foundation model with broad applicability.","evidence_snippet":"“graph transformer encoder” and “masked gene-expression reconstruction”"},{"record_id":"rec_000151","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes multimodal chemical-screening analysis frameworks for decoding perturbation effects, not a generative model. It is a methods paper about screening and inference, with no foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“we develop MoCAVI, a contrastive analysis framework” and “PERCISTRA, a pipeline that infers causal links”"},{"record_id":"rec_000152","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"H2O is presented as a generalist foundation model trained on a very large pan-tissue paired dataset and used to infer spatial transcriptomics and proteomics from histology. The abstract explicitly emphasizes broad generalizability and computational generation of omics landscapes.","evidence_snippet":"“a foundation model bridging histopathology to spatial multi-omics profiling” and “trained on a pan-tissue dataset of 1.3 million paired H&E-spatial patches”"}]}
