urpose-built multimodal training data from thousands of human tumors”"},{"record_id":"rec_000108","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a scoping review of 20 studies, not a primary model report. The mentions of LLM and foundation models are survey content rather than evidence for a candidate generative model.","evidence_snippet":"“This scoping review systematically maps AI- and DL-based methodologies”"},{"record_id":"rec_000109","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly describes a “conditional variational autoencoder framework,” which is a genuinely generative architecture. It presents a task-specific virtual cell model, but not clear foundation-model-like broad pretraining or applicability.","evidence_snippet":"“a lightweight conditional variational autoencoder framework”"},{"record_id":"rec_000110","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model is described as a “modernized BERT-style back-bone,” which is encoder-style rather than clearly generative. The abstract does give foundation-model evidence through genomic sequence modeling and benchmark performance.","evidence_snippet":"“modernized BERT-style back-bone ... adapted to genomic sequence modeling”"},{"record_id":"rec_000111","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract states that the authors performed a “systematic review” of AI-based prognostic models. It summarizes existing recurrence and RFS prediction studies rather than describing a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“We performed a contemporary systematic review”"},{"record_id":"rec_000112","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract applies pre-trained immune system models and a peripheral immune system encoder to predict response and toxicity. This is an application of existing foundation-like models, not a new generative model.","evidence_snippet":"“pre-trained immunotype models” and “a peripheral immune system encoder trained on the BostonGene patient database”"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1658:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:2164:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2606:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0011.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000081","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review that summarizes AI applications in cardio-oncology, not a new generative model. It discusses predictive modeling and implementation challenges rather than foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review synthesizes how artificial intelligence (AI) is redefining cardio-oncology\"; \"review will summarize the current state of emerging applications of machine learning and AI\""},{"record_id":"rec_000082","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes three AI foundation models trained on large public datasets and applied across cohorts, which supports foundation-model-like evidence. The described tasks are predictive/representational, not clearly generative.","evidence_snippet":"\"three AI foundation models\"; \"initially trained on large-scale publicly available datasets\"; \"developed a genomic foundation model ... to predict gene expression\""},{"record_id":"rec_000083","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an AI system for targeted drug delivery using machine learning, deep learning, and reinforcement learning, but no generative architecture is described. The abstract does not provide foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"an ai-based system of targeted drug delivery\"; \"machine learning, deep learning and reinforcement learning in a single system\""},{"record_id":"rec_000084","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper is a diagnostic/methodological study about existing genomic foundation models, not a generative model itself. It does, however, explicitly involve broad foundation models with zero-shot use and cross-architecture analysis.","evidence_snippet":"\"Across three architecturally distinct foundation models\"; \"sequence foundation models offer a zero-shot route\""},{"record_id":"rec_000085","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic review of explainable AI in malaria prediction. The abstract discusses ensemble and deep-learning classifiers, not a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This systematic review synthesises\"; \"ensemble learning models, particularly Random Forest and XGBoost\""},{"record_id":"rec_000086","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a narrative review of machine learning methods and applications in healthcare. It mentions foundation models as a topic, but does not present a new generative model or model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"This narrative review explains the principles of machine learning\"; \"Evidence ... is discussed alongside ... foundation models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000087","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents an end-to-end platform that combines a pretrained patient representation model with an LLM-driven workflow, which reads as an application layer rather than a new generative model. It does provide foundation-model evidence through large-scale pretraining on millions of cells and patients.","evidence_snippet":"\"a patient representation model trained on over 20 million cells across 4,479 patients\"; \"a large language model-driven workflow\""},{"record_id":"rec_000088","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Haiku is a new tri-modal contrastive learning model, but the abstract does not describe a genuinely generative architecture. Its large-scale training and zero-shot biomarker inference support foundation-model-like characteristics.","evidence_snippet":"\"a tri-modal contrastive learning model trained on multiplexed immunofluorescence\"; \"supports zero-shot biomarker inference\""}]}
